    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "s = \"lee(t(c)o)de)\"    ->  \"lee(t(c)o)de\"\ns = \"a)b(c)d(\"          ->  \"ab(c)d\"\ns = \"))((\"              ->  \"\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: remove exactly the brackets that can't be matched"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Some brackets can never be part of a valid string: a `)` with no open `(` before it, and a `(` that is still open when the string ends. Every other bracket can stay. Removing exactly the unmatchable ones is therefore the **minimum** — and finding them is the stack's job, since a `)` always closes the **most recent** open `(`."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Because positions matter (we must know *which* `(` to delete at the end), the stack holds **indexes**, not characters."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Two passes with a counter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A counter is enough if you scan twice. Left to right, drop each `)` that arrives when nothing is open. Then whatever is still open are extra `(` — scanning right to left, drop that many `(` from the end."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function minRemoveToMakeValid(s) {\n  // Pass 1, left to right: drop every ')' with no '(' before it.\n  const kept = [];\n  let balance = 0;\n  for (const ch of s) {\n    if (ch === \"(\") balance++;\n    else if (ch === \")\") {\n      if (balance === 0) continue;\n      balance--;\n    }\n    kept.push(ch);\n  }\n  // Pass 2, right to left: drop the last 'balance' unmatched '('.\n  const out = [];\n  for (let i = kept.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    if (kept[i] === \"(\" && balance > 0) {\n      balance--;\n      continue;\n    }\n    out.push(kept[i]);\n  }\n  return out.reverse().join(\"\");\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def min_remove_to_make_valid(s):\n    # Pass 1, left to right: drop every ')' with no '(' before it.\n    kept = []\n    balance = 0\n    for ch in s:\n        if ch == \"(\":\n            balance += 1\n        elif ch == \")\":\n            if balance == 0:\n                continue\n            balance -= 1\n        kept.append(ch)\n    # Pass 2, right to left: drop the last 'balance' unmatched '('.\n    out = []\n    for ch in reversed(kept):\n        if ch == \"(\" and balance > 0:\n            balance -= 1\n            continue\n        out.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(reversed(out))"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "String minRemoveToMakeValid(String s) {\n    // Pass 1, left to right: drop every ')' with no '(' before it.\n    StringBuilder kept = new StringBuilder();\n    int balance = 0;\n    for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) {\n        if (ch == '(') balance++;\n        else if (ch == ')') {\n            if (balance == 0) continue;\n            balance--;\n        }\n        kept.append(ch);\n    }\n    // Pass 2, right to left: drop the last 'balance' unmatched '('.\n    StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();\n    for (int i = kept.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n        if (kept.charAt(i) == '(' && balance > 0) {\n            balance--;\n            continue;\n        }\n        out.append(kept.charAt(i));\n    }\n    return out.reverse().toString();\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "string minRemoveToMakeValid(string s) {\n    // Pass 1, left to right: drop every ')' with no '(' before it.\n    string kept;\n    int balance = 0;\n    for (char ch : s) {\n        if (ch == '(') balance++;\n        else if (ch == ')') {\n            if (balance == 0) continue;\n            balance--;\n        }\n        kept += ch;\n    }\n    // Pass 2, right to left: drop the last 'balance' unmatched '('.\n    string out;\n    for (int i = (int)kept.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n        if (kept[i] == '(' && balance > 0) {\n            balance--;\n            continue;\n        }\n        out += kept[i];\n    }\n    reverse(out.begin(), out.end());\n    return out;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(n).** Two linear passes and two builders. Dropping the **last** extra `(` is always safe: none of them has a `)` after it waiting to be matched."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. One pass with a stack of indexes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Push the index of every `(`. A `)` pops the most recent one — a match — or, if the stack is empty, is marked for removal. Whatever indexes remain on the stack at the end are unclosed `(`: mark those too, then build the string without the marked positions."
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "min-remove-parentheses",
      "caption": "The stack holds indexes of open '('; unmatched ')' and leftover '(' are greyed out and removed."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function minRemoveToMakeValid(s) {\n  const chars = [...s];\n  const open = [];                            // indexes of '(' still waiting for a match\n  for (let i = 0; i < chars.length; i++) {\n    if (chars[i] === \"(\") open.push(i);\n    else if (chars[i] === \")\") {\n      if (open.length > 0) open.pop();        // matches the most recent '('\n      else chars[i] = \"\";                     // nothing to match: remove it\n    }\n  }\n  for (const i of open) chars[i] = \"\";        // '(' never matched: remove them too\n  return chars.join(\"\");\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def min_remove_to_make_valid(s):\n    chars = list(s)\n    opens = []                            # indexes of '(' still waiting for a match\n    for i, ch in enumerate(chars):\n        if ch == \"(\":\n            opens.append(i)\n        elif ch == \")\":\n            if opens:\n                opens.pop()               # matches the most recent '('\n            else:\n                chars[i] = \"\"             # nothing to match: remove it\n    for i in opens:\n        chars[i] = \"\"                     # '(' never matched: remove them too\n    return \"\".join(chars)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "String minRemoveToMakeValid(String s) {\n    boolean[] remove = new boolean[s.length()];\n    Deque<Integer> open = new ArrayDeque<>();    // indexes of '(' still waiting for a match\n    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n        char ch = s.charAt(i);\n        if (ch == '(') open.push(i);\n        else if (ch == ')') {\n            if (!open.isEmpty()) open.pop();     // matches the most recent '('\n            else remove[i] = true;               // nothing to match: remove it\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i : open) remove[i] = true;         // '(' never matched: remove them too\n    StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();\n    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (!remove[i]) out.append(s.charAt(i));\n    return out.toString();\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "string minRemoveToMakeValid(string s) {\n    vector<int> open;                            // indexes of '(' still waiting for a match\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {\n        if (s[i] == '(') open.push_back(i);\n        else if (s[i] == ')') {\n            if (!open.empty()) open.pop_back();  // matches the most recent '('\n            else s[i] = '*';                     // nothing to match: mark it for removal\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i : open) s[i] = '*';               // '(' never matched: mark them too\n    s.erase(remove(s.begin(), s.end(), '*'), s.end());   // drop every mark in one pass\n    return s;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(n).** One scan, a final pass over the leftover indexes, and one pass to build the answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Two passes with a counter",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "**Two linear passes**: drop extra `)` left to right, extra `(` right to left.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The **string builders**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "One pass with a stack of indexes",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "One scan, then one pass over the **leftover indexes** and one to build.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The stack and the answer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Both are linear. The stack version names the unmatched brackets exactly, which makes it easy to explain why the removal is minimal; the counter version shows you only needed a count, not the whole stack, as long as you scan twice."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**No brackets** — the string is already valid.",
        "**Only closing brackets first** — `\"))((\"`: everything goes.",
        "**Letters everywhere** — letters are never removed.",
        "**Several valid answers** — `\"())\"` can keep either `)`; any valid answer of maximum length is accepted, so test by checking validity and length, not one fixed string."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Valid Parentheses** — just decide whether a string is already valid (Stack course).",
        "**Minimum Add to Make Parentheses Valid** — count instead of remove: unmatched `)` plus `(` left open.",
        "**Remove Invalid Parentheses** — return **all** valid results with the fewest removals: BFS or backtracking over removals (a hard follow-up)."
      ]
    }
  ],
